  "source_findings": [
    "A default-disabled import calls store_transcript_turns without on_stored; B disabled native parse may try per-process tail or full bootstrap with optional on_stored.",
    "B _try_tail refuses no_frontier before loading a durable CP when this process-local frontier is missing. Native decide(no_checkpoint) is not necessarily the first route.",
    "Both _write_checkpoint implementations call on_stored with actual database, not ImportWriter; probe snapshot can upgrade/write CP without taking locked replay.",
    "B CP/bootstrap publication conditional on unchanged input identity, safe boundary/effect predicate/carry and native final checkpoint checks. Missing CP cannot choose zero policy for a required-publication route.",
    "An unchanged-row full parse does not establish no DB writes: CP callback can write. A CP write does not prove message allocations or locked replay occurred.",
    "Conditional no-mutation A/no-callback native probe has one BEGIN/COMMIT on that connection; B successful single CP savepoint on same probe adds SAVEPOINT/RELEASE. These are selected boundary shapes, NOT total bank or actor bounds.",
    "Probe WriteNeeded is a normal native transition: original read transaction rolls back, then locked revalidation/replay occurs. Locked batches can yield by elapsed hold time as well as sequence.",
    "Callback exceptions can be logged/rolled back behind savepoint while outer import still returns; import return alone cannot prove CP publication or classify all work/counters.",
    "Real raw seed payload/client-provenance/summary/tie/state and all actual writers/retries/connection lifetimes remain unproved; no actual row mutation/resource bound follows from these source paths."
  ]
